Design a binary encoder that converts a 2-bit input D into a 3-bit output C. Upon the rising edge of the clock, the module first captures the input D and then shifts it left by one position, while filling the least significant bit with zero, effectively encoding the input into a wider output format. The final output C will always represent the binary value of the input D, expanded to a 3-bit wide signal.
module top_module(
    input [1:0] D,
    input clk, // Added clk as an input
    output reg [2:0] C
);

