description:
Design a synchronizer module that minimizes metastability issues when transferring an asynchronous input signal (async_in) to a synchronous output (sync_out) using a clock input (clk_in). The module utilizes a two-stage flip-flop mechanism, first capturing the asynchronous input in an intermediate register (async_sync) on the rising edge of the clock, and then updating the output (sync_out) based on the stabilized signal from the first stage. This design ensures that the output reflects the state of the asynchronous signal in a stable and synchronized manner.
module top_module(
  input async_in,
  input clk_in,
  output reg sync_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input async_in,
  input clk_in,
  output reg sync_out
);reg async_sync;
  reg async_sync_prev;

  always @(posedge clk_in) begin
    async_sync_prev <= async_sync;
    async_sync <= async_in;
  end

  always @(posedge clk_in) begin
    if (clk_in) begin
      sync_out <= async_sync;
    end else begin
      sync_out <= async_sync_prev;
    end
  end

endmodule

